From: Mitchell Augustin <mitchell.augustin@canonical.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Feb 2025 11:31:00 -0600
Subject: remote-desktop, desktop-sharing: Handle when keyring is locked
The desktop sharing credentials can't be loaded neither stored when the
session keyring is locked.

So let's show a permission banner asking the user to "Unlock" and keep
the Login Details widgets sensitive when locked.

This will prevent the password from being incorrectly overwritten with
a randomly generated default once it has already been set.

Origin: backport, https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-control-center/-/commit/334c2a076e22295dbf46b7d1849e1ebb1f8d897d
Origin: backport, https://gitlab.gnome.org/aleasto/gnome-control-center/-/commit/5940af5b204d62de68e67258ea7551abb1d8219b
Bug: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-control-center/-/issues/3547
Author: Alessandro Astone <alessandro.astone@canonical.com>
